<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<odoo noupdate="1">

    <record id="channel_event_logistics" model="slide.channel">
        <field name="name">Logistics Lead</field>
        <field name="channel_type">training</field>
        <field name="description" type="html">
            <p>Permits, temporary staff, crew bookings, facilities, and
            reading the Logistics tab's readiness numbers.</p>
        </field>
        <field name="visibility">members</field>
        <field name="enroll">invite</field>
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="enroll_group_ids" eval="[(6, 0, [ref('event.group_event_user')])]" />
    </record>

    <!-- ===================== Section 1: Permits ===================== -->
    <record id="section_permits" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_logistics" />
        <field name="name">Permits</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">10</field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_checklist" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_logistics" />
        <field name="name">Building a permit checklist from an event type</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">11</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <p>For a recurring event (an annual festival), add a
            <strong>Permit Checklist</strong> to its Event Type once - a
            name, permit type, and how many days before the event it should
            be submitted by. Then on any event of that type, click
            <strong>Generate permits from event type</strong> on the
            Logistics tab and the whole list appears with submit-by dates
            already calculated - it skips anything already generated, so
            it's safe to click more than once.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_permit_deadlines" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_logistics" />
        <field name="name">Submit-by and expiry reminders</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">12</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <p>A permit moves through Not Started → Submitted →
            Approved (or Denied). A daily check flags two situations
            automatically with a to-do for the responsible person: a
            not-started permit whose submit-by date is approaching, and an
            approved permit whose expiry date is coming up for renewal. You
            don't have to track either on a separate calendar.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- ============= Section 2: Temporary staff & crews ============= -->
    <record id="section_staff" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_logistics" />
        <field name="name">Temporary staff &amp; crews</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">20</field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_staff_shifts" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_logistics" />
        <field name="name">Staff shifts and check-in/out</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">21</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <p>A <strong>Staff Shift</strong> is a role (Security, Setup
            Crew, Ushers…), a time window, and how many people you
            need. Add workers to it as they're hired - each gets
            <strong>Check In</strong> / <strong>Check Out</strong> buttons
            that compute their hours automatically, the same shape as
            volunteer shifts, but for paid workers. There's no Community
            Edition payroll app to hand those hours to, so this stops at
            producing clean hours worked for whoever runs payroll
            externally.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_crew_bookings" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_logistics" />
        <field name="name">Crew bookings and day-of contacts</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">22</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <p>A <strong>Crew Booking</strong> records the vendor or crew
            (stage, sound, security, sanitation, generator, tent…),
            load-in and load-out times, and - the part a purchase order
            never captures - a <strong>day-of contact name and phone</strong>,
            since whoever shows up on the truck often isn't who signed the
            contract. A Purchase Order link is optional, since not every
            booking runs through formal procurement (an in-kind sponsor,
            for instance). Move it through Planned → Confirmed →
            On Site → Complete as the day unfolds.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- ============ Section 3: Facilities & readiness ============ -->
    <record id="section_facilities" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_logistics" />
        <field name="name">Facilities &amp; readiness</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">30</field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_facilities" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_logistics" />
        <field name="name">Placing facilities on the vendor map</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">31</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <p>Add a <strong>Facility</strong> for each portable toilet
            cluster, hand-wash station, first-aid tent, or similar - a
            type, a quantity, and optionally which Crew Booking services
            it. If the venue map module is installed, open the event's
            Vendor Map and click <strong>Place Facilities</strong> to arm a
            facility, then click the map where it actually sits - the same
            live map vendor booths use, just a second pin layer.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_readiness" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_logistics" />
        <field name="name">The Logistics tab and the readiness reminder</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">32</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <p>The event's <strong>Logistics</strong> tab shows four
            numbers at a glance: permits approved/total, staffing filled
            percentage, crews confirmed/total, and a facility count. A
            daily check, starting two weeks before the event by default,
            raises <strong>one</strong> consolidated to-do for the Logistics
            Coordinator if anything's still open - a single message listing
            what's outstanding, not a separate notification per issue.
            Three printable reports (Permit Status, Staffing Roster, and a
            combined Crew &amp; Facilities Day-Of Sheet) round out what you
            can hand to your team.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- ========================= Quiz ========================= -->
    <record id="slide_quiz" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_event_logistics" />
        <field name="name">Check your understanding</field>
        <field name="slide_category">quiz</field>
        <field name="sequence">90</field>
    </record>

    <record id="quiz_q1" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="question">A permit is Not Started and its submit-by date is approaching. What happens?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">Nothing - you have to track deadlines yourself</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">A daily check raises a to-do for the responsible person</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">The permit is automatically marked Denied</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">The event is cancelled automatically</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>

    <record id="quiz_q2" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="question">Does a crew booking require a linked Purchase Order?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">Yes, always</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">No - it's optional, since not every booking is a formal purchase</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">Only for sound and stage bookings</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">Only once the crew is marked On Site</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>

    <record id="quiz_q3" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="question">If three things are open (a permit, a shift, a crew booking) two weeks before an event, how many to-dos does the readiness check raise?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">Three - one per open item</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">One consolidated to-do listing all of them</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">None - it only runs the day of the event</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">One per day until it's resolved</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>

    <record id="quiz_q4" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="question">Where do you place a facility's pin on the map?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">A separate facilities-only map</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">The same live Vendor Map, using Place Facilities mode</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">You can't - facilities have no location</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">On the crew booking's own form only</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>

</odoo>
